==Original Issue==
In settings there is a checkbox about whether you continue to the end and there's the slider for the UI and they seem to actually function in terms of doing what they're supposed to do to the UI but they themselves when you're moving them around don't seem to be able to update in the actual settings activity So it looks like you're doing nothing while you're in there but then when you go back out of the settings it turns out that they've gone into effect and then if you go back into the settings they're now displaying their correct values so there's some sort of state that they're not able to update their appearance

==Status Report: 2026-10-12 00:10 PDT==
IMPLEMENTED (builds + tests pass).

Root cause: `SettingsScreen` received `continuity` and `playerBarScale` as plain,
immutable parameters captured once from the store. Toggling the checkbox or
moving the slider wrote to `SettingsStore` (via the callbacks), but nothing
recomposed the checkbox/slider — so the controls only "caught up" after you left
and re-entered Settings.

Fix: the two values are now held in Compose state inside `SettingsScreen`
(`remember { mutableStateOf(...) }`, initialized from the store values). Each
control update writes BOTH the local state (so it redraws immediately) AND the
store (via the existing callbacks), so appearance and persisted value stay in
sync while you're still on the screen.

Files: `SettingsActivity.kt` only.

Verified: `./gradlew assembleDebug` and `testDebugUnitTest` pass. Please
confirm on-device that the checkbox and slider now update immediately while the
Settings screen is open. 